cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Duckoder
message: If you use Duckoder in your work, please cite the monograph below.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Web platform that generates code for teaching boards, such as the ESP32 and the Arduino Uno,
  Mega and Nano, from requests written in Brazilian Portuguese. The code is generated by the
  Claude API or by a language model running locally through Ollama, from a hardware profile that
  describes the board's components and pins.
authors:
  - given-names: José Vinícius
    family-names: Alves de Oliveira
    alias: ctrl-vini
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.4.0
date-released: '2026-10-18'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ctrl-vini/duckoder'
url: 'https://www.duckoder.com.br'
keywords:
  - embedded systems
  - ESP32
  - Arduino
  - large language models
  - code generation
  - computing education

# The work the software belongs to; GitHub's citation box offers this one.
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: >-
    Plataforma web com LLM local para apoio à programação de sistemas embarcados
    didáticos
  authors:
    - given-names: José Vinícius
      family-names: Alves de Oliveira
  year: 2026
  institution:
    name: Instituto Federal de Educação, Ciência e Tecnologia do Ceará
    city: Jaguaribe
    country: BR
  thesis-type: >-
